#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "126c85b8-d721-5e7d-a3dc-df997bc0b9ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-4732" :question/problem "Consider $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$.\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A$, is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + 7R_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary\nrow operation\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+7R_3\n$$\n\nto $A$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "f8eb89c4-1cca-5f8c-909c-31e9e0fc8412" :question/math-academy-id "e-4733" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation\n\n$$\nR_2:= R_2-2R_1\n$$\n\nto $A$.\n\nTo find $E$, we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} - 2R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "6e47a532-ba7a-5692-961b-eabc743d74e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4734" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$:\n$R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad R_1:=6R_1$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid ↔R_{3}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{1}$\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid:=6R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{2}$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A$, we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A$, we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba0dc318-99c3-5735-961e-d96ede3eda12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131083} {:answer/id #uuid "ce205d22-d75c-5936-b652-e1e0097a6bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131084} {:answer/id #uuid "d36ed1aa-b0a1-50f6-8b61-44937ae34753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131085} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9b60a4-7de6-5e2c-be99-0cc08efb2e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131086} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff700c9-9504-5db3-b15d-0b1388d30094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba0dc318-99c3-5735-961e-d96ede3eda12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131083} :answer-field/id #uuid "b84dd032-6c72-58de-967d-2588734e0a43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131082}] :question/id #uuid "5850f9b5-76bb-54cc-bfaa-176ac2b82ca9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32128" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 3R_{3}$ is applied to a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80b45b10-8cee-58cc-9371-2350693e88f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=2R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131101} {:answer/id #uuid "a440ece5-02ce-5ce2-85e9-1db00626b517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{1}↔R_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131102} {:answer/id #uuid "a84cacac-b27c-5082-bb04-daf0338f909d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{1}↔R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131103} {:answer/id #uuid "c1673f30-3dcf-5693-981a-f57ffcbd3a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{1}:=R_{1} + R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131104} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc44fd2-5515-5610-8ff2-135c449d582f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}:=R_{3} - R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a84cacac-b27c-5082-bb04-daf0338f909d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{1}↔R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131103} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f0993b-b981-5a2c-94c5-f8439756c57a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131100}] :question/id #uuid "67780f7b-b335-51d6-8512-e61d1ae7ee4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32147" :question/problem "Consider $E = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$.\n\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A$, is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left."}]}
